            <ArticleTitle>ACS chemical neuroscience molecule spotlight on Valdoxen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>772-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/cn100062j</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new and novel non-SSRI potential treatment option for major depressive disorders is Valdoxen (agomelatine) which is currently in phase III clinical studies. Valdoxen is a norepinephrine disinhibitor (NNDI) and is also an antagonist of the 5-HT(2C) receptor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
